From 6377511f262890d55560a7a02e971b98651f7271 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:00:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(compression): never anchor a request whose turn
 already ended

Problem: on 2026-11-13 at 11:31 PST, a mid-turn compaction of a background-process turn
(MacBook session 20261026_235722_bef6c6) wrote user row 913645. That row copied update-resume
row 913363: same message_uid, original 11:12:09 timestamp, a 7-card Kanban batch. It landed in
the new tail between the first tool group and the next call. Reply 913453 had already answered
the batch at 11:20:53, and process_complete row 913464 started the running turn. So the model was
handed finished work as its latest ask.

Why 1: _ensure_compressed_has_user_turn (compress_context, run after the engine) put the copy
there. It is not _reappend_inflight_user_task: the row has no "STILL IN PROGRESS" header, keeps
its timestamp, and sits at _insert_real_user_anchor's slot (the first assistant row not preceded
by a user row).
Why 2: when no real user row survives the compaction, that pass anchors the newest real user row
of the original transcript, whether or not that row's turn has ended. 913363 (auto_continue) is a
real user row; 913464 (process_complete) is scaffolding.
Why 3: 65f80f4ff5 made only _find_inflight_user_task turn-aware (turn_ended_after). The second
restoration pass kept the old "newest human row" rule. In this incident _find_inflight_user_task
correctly returned None: the 3 hypotheses on the card are all refuted. In-memory and DB rows
agree, the update-resume row behaves as expected, and 913453 was present.
Root (happened): two passes restore intent after a compaction. Only one of them knew when a turn
ends.
Root (not caught): 65f80f4ff5's end-to-end test drove ContextCompressor.compress(), which never
runs the compress_context anchor pass.

Fix: the anchor scan (agent/context_compressor_turns.py newest_live_intent) stops at the newest
intent-bearing row (a real user row, or a steer riding in a tool result). If that row's turn has
ended, nothing is anchored and the existing no-intent placeholder stands in. A running request (no completed reply yet, or an auto_continue after a
partial reply) is still anchored. Behaviour for #100818 and #80622 is unchanged.

Proof: tests/agent/test_compaction_anchor_ended_turn.py.
- Runs agent._compress_context end to end with a real SessionDB and ContextCompressor. The row
  shapes are 913291..913464, and the process_complete row is staged by
  agent.turn_context._stage_turn_user_message with display_kind=process_complete.
- Results: 3 fail on the base and 7 pass after. The control (an unanswered resumed batch keeps
  one actionable copy) passes on both.
- The existing 65f80f4ff5, #100818, busy-steer, last-assistant-anchor and split-turn suites pass.
